* FDEChecker probably doesn't need to be declared in .h. Allows it to keep stuff like sink etc and simplify stuff internally. Make FDECheckerOptions standalong. Forward-declare FDEChecker. Have CreateFDEChecker that returns unique_ptr with custom deleter. And have standalone CheckFDE function that receives the FDEChecker. Alternative is abstract FDEChecker class or FDECheckerIface or something. And the concrete implementation. Maybe less ceremony around unique_ptr etc.
** actually no. since current fde checker constructor is just storing image/disasm/options etc it is not needed. Just have CheckFDE function call that receives everything. Put image and disasm into options. Then in the .cc we can have FDEChecker with all the state gathered (sink, etc)
